/-!
# The rank-two component argument in Section 15.3

This is the assembly boundary for 15.3.35 and 15.3.39--42, Aschbacher--Smith,
combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed pp.1135 and 1137--1139.

The reductions establish `I = LS` from minimality, the simple generalized
Fitting subgroup in the actual centralizer quotient, its local normalizer,
the strict-containment clause, and the contradiction from an irreducible
radical of order sixteen. The source conclusion and all the local quotient
clauses have explicit definitions for the remaining arguments.

The two-component and rank-one containment arguments, the remaining clauses
of 15.3.41, and the non-characteristic-two and parabolic classifications are
still required. Neither 15.3.35 nor 15.3.39--42 is claimed complete here.
-/
